<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1096 0 R
/E (From the table above we see that the total RWA expanded aggressively from BDT 295.2 Billion in 2021 to BDT 512.0 Billion in 2025. This represents a cumulative increase of 73.4%. The causes of the surge were- expanding corporate loan portfolios, digital retail financing, and trade finance lines. The asset expansion surpassed the Tier-1 capital growth, as Tier-1 capital declined from 11.70% to 9.10%, bringing total CRAR to 13.90%. The bank remained 140 basis points above the regulatory floor, although capital consumption increased.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
524 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1097 0 R
/E (The bank maintained a strong earnings performance consistently across the 5-year period. ROE expanded from 14.80% in 2021 consistently and reached its peak in 2024 at 23.92%, then stabilized at 21.50% in 2025. ROA expanded throughout the years from 1.05% in 2021 to 1.42% in 2025. Robust profit generation resulted in increasing the retained earnings. This increase in retained earnings absorbed the incremental provisioning expenses caused by the rising NPL ratio, which increased to 5.60% in 2025 amid industry-wide credit stress.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
