/E (Money Laundering Prevention Act, 2012: Section 4\(2\) criminalizes converting, transferring, or concealing proceeds of crime. Section 4\(3\) sets penalties up to 12 years imprisonment and monetary fines, holding banking personnel directly liable for assisting illicit fund movement.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [11]
>>
