557 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 141 0 R
/E (Following the incident, City Bank strengthened its compliance framework by expanding its AML department from around 4 to 5 employees to approximately 25 to 30 employees. The bank also invested in automated transaction monitoring and strengthened its sanctions screening and monitoring system to identify suspicious activities and screen customers and beneficiaries against relevant watchlists. These measures can improve early detection and reduce the likelihood of similar incidents. Overall, the case demonstrates that effective banking compliance requires not only advanced technology but also strong internal controls, employee accountability, independent verification, timely reporting, and continuous regulatory oversight.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
